From: MakOS Project <makos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] diagnostics: trace HTTP acceptance continuations by channel

Observe accepted parent/child HTTP loads, classifier dispatch and callbacks,
proxy resolution, suspend/resume and connection entry. Preserve every return,
callback order, ignored-dispatch policy and browser security decision.
Reuse existing 128-attempt admission and single-write transport unchanged.
Only real channel IDs and raw results; zero flags mean metadata unavailable.
Classifier workers use a main-thread snapshot, never off-thread COM getters.
No URL text, retry, forced callback, preference or qualification-limit change.
NS_OK on entry/void boundaries is neutral metadata, not a completed request.

